# pocket-agents configuration. Copy it to config.env (git ignores that file)
# and fill in what you need; every line is optional except where noted.
#
# setup.sh runs on the server through 'bash -s', so it can't ask you anything
# and ssh doesn't carry your local variables across. Put this file in front of
# the script instead:
#
#   cat config.env setup.sh | ssh root@<IP> 'bash -s'    # phase 1
#   cat config.env setup.sh | ssh dev@<IP>  'bash -s'    # phase 2
#
# cloudflare/tunnel-setup.sh runs on the server by hand: it reads config.env
# from the repo root if there is one, and asks for whatever is missing.

# ── setup.sh ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Repos to turn into sessions, with a forge prefix; no prefix means GitHub.
# Empty is fine: 'claude-repos pick' lets you choose them later.
#REPOS="myorg/api gitlab:mygroup/web"

# Runtime versions. NODE_V is a fixed major on purpose; "lts" follows the
# current LTS and can switch majors on a rerun.
#NODE_V=24
#GO_V=1.23
#PY_V=3.12

# OpenAI's Codex and its unit. Off by default.
#CODEX=1

# Free space phase 2 insists on before installing the runtimes, in GB. They
# take about 3; lower it only if you know they fit.
#MIN_FREE_GB=4

# Where phase 2 clones this repo from, if you use a fork.
#SELF_REPO=https://github.com/<you>/pocket-agents.git

# ── cloudflare/tunnel-setup.sh ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Cloudflare zone the previews hang from: p<port>-<LABEL>.<ZONE>.
# Required for the tunnel; asked for if it's missing.
#ZONE=example.com
#LABEL=dev
#TUNNEL=dev-vps
#PORTS="3000 4321 5000 5173 8000 8080 8090"
